ve a  free trade agreement a new way of doing  business with the rest of Europe so you  know there's lots of excitement out  there and we can really move ahead and I  can really see that confidence  throughout the country yes we had Mark  Carney downgrading the growth forecast  obviously for the UK  only earlier today talking about the  Canada deal a nice off-the-shelf model  that people can understand the problem  is that the Treasury's own forecasts had  said it would mean a loss of four point  nine percent to the British economy over  15 years compared to staying in the  European Union and it doesn't include  services that is what more than 80  percent  of our economy well I mean first of all  you just mentioned downgrading forecast  by summon and the the point there is  that there you name you find me a  country anywhere in the world that  hasn't had its forecasts downgraded in  in in recent weeks the last few months  and that's because there is a problem  for the global economy but Britain is  doing well we want it to do better and  that of course means our services  industries our financial services  industry for example is hugely important  in terms of the job and wealth creation  for everyone and it's something that I  know will continue to go from strength  to strength as we leave the EU we strike  a new trade agreement let's talk about  fishing if we can it seems to be the  first great stumbling block that the UK  government and the European Union will  come up against just naught point naught  4 percent of the economy here in the UK  and yet absolutely crucial to the French  president emmanuel micro making clear  that without good trade in fishing that  the rest of it you can forget about  180,000 jobs across the EU block in  fishing alone why are you deciding to  look after fishing at the expense of a  trade deal if you know it's not about  looking after fishing or anything else  it's about looking after Britain and  looking after our interests and that'